skill: social-strategy
version: 1.0.0
description: Scenario tests for social-strategy. A run passes only when every item in 'expect' is satisfied. Written before the skill body (test-first).
evals[8]:
  - name, input, expect
  - happy-path-strategy, Help me build a social media strategy., "reads brand-profile, audience.md, and content-pillars first (or runs them where missing)|sets one primary objective tied to the business, with a meaningful metric|selects 1-3 channels using the fit framework and names what it drops|defines a strategic wedge from the brand's POV|sets a sustainable, phased operating model|writes a social-strategy.md"
  - focus-not-everywhere, "I want to be active on every platform — Instagram, TikTok, LinkedIn, X, YouTube, Pinterest, Facebook.", pushes back on spreading thin|selects the few channels where the audience is and the brand can win|explicitly names which platforms to drop or run as maintenance|recommends starting focused (often one primary channel)
  - channel-fit-framework, Should I be on TikTok?, "answers using audience presence, format fit, goal fit, and capacity — not gut feel|considers whether the brand can sustain video content|gives a clear recommendation with the reasoning"
  - business-goal-not-vanity, My goal is to get to 100k followers., "reframes toward a business-tied objective and a meaningful metric|explains why follower count alone is often a vanity metric|ties the strategy to what the business actually needs (leads, sales, authority, awareness)"
  - honest-measurement, Set up the strategy and tell me how we'll track performance., "sets meaningful metrics and a review cadence|is honest about measurement: WoopSocial post analytics for TikTok, LinkedIn, Facebook, Instagram, Pinterest, YouTube, and Bluesky, native dashboards otherwise|does NOT promise dashboards or automated reporting the product can't deliver|routes detailed target-setting (SMART targets, North Stars, thresholds) to goals-and-kpis"
  - strategic-wedge-required, What's our angle to stand out?, "defines a differentiated wedge from the brand's POV/positioning|does NOT settle for 'post good/consistent content' as the strategy|if positioning is too weak to yield a wedge, says so and points back to brand-profile"
  - realistic-phasing, We're a 2-person team launching on social next month., recommends starting focused (one primary channel) rather than launching everywhere|matches cadence to the team's real capacity|uses repurposing to extend reach without doubling the workload|lays out a phased expansion
  - subtraction-strategy, We're posting on 6 platforms and nothing is really working., recommends consolidating to the 1-2 channels that fit best|treats dropping/demoting channels as a valid strategic move|redirects freed-up effort to winning where it counts
